What was changed
----------------

These files are not the source meshes. The pipeline in build/anatomy/ does the following, and
every step is reproducible from the scripts there:

  * selects named parts by FMA identifier (see build/anatomy/parts.py)
  * resolves composite parts — the heart, brain and lungs have no mesh of their own and are
    defined as unions of primitives — and concatenates them
  * removes stray disconnected shells; for the skin, keeps only the outer body surface, which
    arrives as one shell among 31,130
  * decimates to a web triangle budget (32,000 faces for the body; fewer for organs)
  * applies a similarity transform — mirror in X, uniform scale, translation — fitted to
    aortic landmarks, mapping the source's millimetre coordinates into this project's scene
    frame (see build/anatomy/fit_transform.py and transform.json)

Because CC BY-SA is share-alike, these derived meshes carry the same licence. Anyone reusing
them must keep this notice and licence them alike. The repository's own source code remains
under the MIT licence in the root LICENSE file.

Vessel centerlines in build/anatomy/vessels.json are likewise derived from this source and
carry the same licence and attribution.
